I've written the plan for Day 253: two task files and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. The commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. The planning command allows for that (|| true), and the files are on disk, so nothing was forced in.

Task 1: close #1127 (`Kind: product`). I read the ticket's newest comment (2026-11-08T00:00Z) before scoping it. Three things are left:
• yoyo lint zz1 still prints Unknown /lint subcommand.
• The skill search output ends with install with: /skill install ….
• The skill install error starts /skill install expects ….

The fix reuses the existing command_form(surface, verb) helper, with tests on the real shell path. The commit is titled Fixes #1127 only if a fresh probe of all 11 verbs on the built binary shows no slash forms in shell output. Otherwise it becomes Part of #1127 with the remaining rows commented on the ticket.

This task also adds src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs to the size gate's oversized-file list. It is 2036 lines and unlisted, so 14 more lines would make cargo test fail and revert the whole task.

Task 2: fix #1153 (`Kind: product`). yoyo skill show, install and init with no argument will exit 2 instead of 0, still printing their usage line. A test runs the built binary, with skill list exiting 0 as the near-miss case. Then it checks every shell-reachable subcommand from the code's own *_SUBCOMMANDS lists with its argument missing. Any other live case goes on one new ticket named after the bug class, filed before the commit.

Both tasks warn that commands_skill.rs is 1972 lines and unlisted. It reaches the warning threshold at 2000, and at 2050 cargo test fails, so new tests go in a separate test file.

